@startuml sequence_set_thermostat
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title User sets thermostat (HTTP request + SignalR event)\nPresentation widget emits (submit); container component calls IBackendClient

actor User
participant "ThermostatControl\n(components lib)" as TC
participant "DashboardComponent\n(container, smart-building-demo)" as Dash
participant "IBackendClient\n(impl: BackendClient @ api)" as BC
participant "BFF" as BFF
participant "Backend Mesh" as Mesh
participant "BFF Hub" as Hub
participant "IRoomStateStore\n(impl: RoomStateStore @ api)" as RS
participant "Snackbar" as Snack

User -> TC: select room R-101, set 22 C, Submit
TC -> Dash: (submit) emits { roomId: "R-101", targetC: 22 }
Dash -> BC: request<SetThermostatAck>("Contracts.Requests.SetThermostat",\n  { roomId: "R-101", targetC: 22 })
BC -> BFF: POST /api/requests
BFF -> Mesh: dispatch via RedisBus (Control -> Actuator)
Mesh --> BFF: SetThermostatAck { roomId, deviceId, effectiveC: 22 }
BFF --> BC: 200 { ack }
BC --> Dash: ack
Dash -> Snack: open("Applied 22 C to R-101")

== broadcast event reaches the same SPA ==

Mesh -> BFF: PUBLISH evt.Contracts.ThermostatChanged
BFF -> Hub: OnMessage("evt.Contracts.ThermostatChanged", envelope)
Hub -> RS: merge ThermostatChanged
RS -> Dash: rooms$ emits updated room
Dash -> TC: [rooms] Input refreshed
TC --> User: table row reflects new effectiveC

@enduml
